3a03258ad0f694b585240fc110476f0dce2aa9d990651","file":"preprints/Optimal-order-mixing-of-the-Thorp-shuffle-September-26-2026/build/main.tex","line":53,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"ece65a97f824ad8f21152a8a1f81c3cfc5dc5984dbe266f0b34d5616493558f8","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Optimal-order-mixing-of-the-Thorp-shuffle-September-26-2026/build/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:5f90c57327b263b2f693a03258ad0f694b585240fc110476f0dce2aa9d990651","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Optimal-order-mixing-of-the-Thorp-shuffle-September-26-2026/build/main.tex#L53"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:mixing}\nAs $d\\to\\infty$,\n\\[\n \\|q_d^{*(1600d)}-U_n\\|_{\\mathrm{TV}}\\longrightarrow0.\n\\]\nFor every integer $t\\ge0$,\n\\[\n \\|q_d^{*t}-U_n\\|_{\\mathrm{TV}}\n \\ge 1-\\frac{2^{tn/2}}{n!}.\n\\]\nConsequently the mixing time at distance $1/4$ satisfies\n\\[\n t_{\\mathrm{mix}}(d)\\ge\n \\left\\lceil\\frac2n\\log_2\\frac{3n!}{4}\\right\\rceil\n =2d-O(1),\n \\qquad t_{\\mathrm{mix}}(d)=\\Theta(d).\n\\]"}
